From: Claude Assistant <assistant@example.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 23:56:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Task 2: add shared cross-app nav bar across all four
 Project Signal apps

- Dashboard, Triage, Assistant, and Allocation each linked to one
  another via a consistent top nav strip (matching the existing dark
  theme / IBM Plex Mono styling), so the four HTML deliverables read
  as one connected product instead of four standalone demos.
- Current app is highlighted with the existing amber accent color,
  consistent with the tab-active styling already used elsewhere.
- Confirmed (no change needed): shared vs. personal storage is
  already correctly distinguished in the UI - triage_reviews uses
  window.storage(..., shared=false) since it's per-reviewer, while
  the assistant's review_queue and allocation's decision/audit-log
  storage use shared=true and are already labelled '(shared)' in
  their headings.
---
 scripts/project_signal_allocation.html | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 scripts/project_signal_assistant.html  | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 scripts/project_signal_dashboard.html  | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 scripts/project_signal_triage.html     | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 64 insertions(+)

diff --git a/scripts/project_signal_allocation.html b/scripts/project_signal_allocation.html
index e202b44..cd2dbee 100644
